From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Add 3 AVPs from 3GPP TS 29.329
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

3GPP TS 29.329 V18.0.0 defines these AVPs in vendor 10415, which the
dictionary has no entry for at their codes:

  Call-Reference-Info (720): Grouped, 2 members, clause 6.3.29
  Call-Reference-Number (721): OctetString, clause 6.3.30
  AS-Number (722): OctetString, clause 6.3.31

Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

Generated by Seanchaí (integrations/wireshark/additions.py).
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml
index 65e5a13..dc8a49e 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/TGPP.xml
@@ -1098,6 +1098,18 @@
     <enum name="RAT-Type-Requested" code="2"/>
     <!-- <enum name="Location-Information-EPS-Supported,RAT-Type-Requested" code="3"/> -->
   </avp>
+  <avp name="Call-Reference-Info" code="720" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+    <grouped>
+      <gavp name="Call-Reference-Number"/>
+      <gavp name="AS-Number"/>
+    </grouped>
+  </avp>
+  <avp name="Call-Reference-Number" code="721" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+    <type type-name="OctetString"/>
+  </avp>
+  <avp name="AS-Number" code="722" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="must" may-encrypt="no" vendor-id="TGPP">
+    <type type-name="OctetString"/>
+  </avp>
   <!--
   720 Call-Reference-Info Grouped
   721 Call-Reference-Number OctetString
